# SRG-APP-000177-AU-002650  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must map the authenticated identity to the
# individual user or group account for PKI-based authentication.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000177-AU-002650
group:           V-206480
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000187
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk extracts an identity from the presented certificate by a configured
                 method and OID list, and maps that identity to Splunk roles through the
                 role map stanza for the authentication strategy, which is the whole of the
                 mapping the product performs.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod in CommonName|EDIPI|PIV
check:           authentication.conf [roleMap_<authSettings-key>] <Splunk RoleName> non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthPivOidList https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthPivOidList non_empty
                 reason: 10.4.2 spec: "A list of object identifiers (OIDs) that the Splunk
                         platform uses to lookup an end-user's PIV info in the Subject
                         Alternate Name extension of the client certificate... Default:
                         1.3.6.1.4.1.311.20.2.3, Microsoft Universal Principal Name,
                         Microsoft User Principal Name". The CAC page gives the default as
                         "1.3.6.1.4.1.311.20.2.3, Microsoft Universal Principal Name" and
                         says multiple OIDs are comma-separated.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The certificate profile that populates the Common Name, EDIPI or PIV OID
                 the application reads
external:        The directory service or identity provider that holds the group
                 memberships the role map refers to, and the account the extracted identity
                 resolves to
external:        Whether each mapped group corresponds to the intended individual or group
                 account is an account management decision

citation:        SRG-APP-000177-AU-002650 check text; web.conf.spec:133-143
                 (certBasedUserAuthMethod: CommonName, EDIPI or PIV; no default),
                 web.conf.spec:144-150 (certBasedUserAuthPivOidList, the OIDs queried in
                 the Subject Alternate Name, with a default OID set),
                 authentication.conf.spec:351-360 ([roleMap_<authSettings-key>] holds
                 role-to-group mappings for the named strategy, each entry a <Splunk
                 RoleName> with a semicolon-separated list)
finding:         web.conf does not set a certificate identity extraction method with an OID
                 list, or authentication.conf has no role map entry for the authentication
                 strategy in use, so the application does not map the PKI-authenticated
                 identity to an individual user or group account.
